  Let's write a comprehensive, clear, and structured documentation of `src/tree.h`.# AST Node Structure (`src/tree.h`) Documentation
  
  The AST in **shish** is built around a single polymorphic container type, **`union node`** (typedef'd as **`node_t`**), tagged by an **`enum kind`** identifier (`id`).
  
  All nodes in a sequence or statement list are linked using a single-linked list pattern via the **`next`** pointer member present at the same offset in every node structure.
  
  ---
  
  ## 1. Node Tag Enum (`enum kind`)
  
  Nodes are broadly grouped into three major functional categories:
  
  ### A. Commands & Control Flow
  * **`N_SIMPLECMD`** (`0`): Simple command execution (`struct ncmd`).
  * **`N_PIPELINE`**: Command pipeline (`struct npipe`).
  * **`N_NOT`**: Pipeline exit status negation (`struct nnot`).
  * **`N_AND`**, **`N_OR`**: Logical conditional lists (`struct nandor`).
  * **`N_LIST`**: Sequence list of commands (`struct nlist`).
  * **`N_SUBSHELL`**: Subshell execution `( ... )` (`struct ngrp`).
  * **`N_BRACEGROUP`**: Group command `{ ...; }` (`struct ngrp`).
  * **`N_FOR`**: `for` loop construct (`struct nfor`).
  * **`N_CASE`**: `case` statement (`struct ncase`).
  * **`N_CASENODE`**: Individual pattern match clause in `case` (`struct ncasenode`).
  * **`N_IF`**: `if` / `elif` / `else` conditional (`struct nif`).
  * **`N_WHILE`**, **`N_UNTIL`**: `while` and `until` loops (`struct nloop`).
  * **`N_FUNCTION`**: Shell function definition (`struct nfunc`).
  
  ### B. Words, Expansions & Redirections
  * **`N_ARG`**: Word argument containing a linked list of expansion pieces (`struct narg`).
  * **`N_ASSIGN`**: Variable assignment prefix (e.g. `VAR=val`) (`struct narg`).
  * **`N_REDIR`**: I/O Redirection descriptor (`struct nredir`).
  * **`N_ARGSTR`**: Literal string / text token segment (`struct nargstr`).
  * **`N_ARGCMD`**: Command substitution `$(...)` or `` `...` `` (`struct nargcmd`).
  * **`N_ARGPARAM`**: Parameter expansion `$VAR`, `${VAR...}` (`struct nargparam`).
  * **`N_ARGARITH`**: Arithmetic expansion `$((...))` (`struct nargarith`).
  
  ### C. Arithmetic AST Nodes
  * **`A_NUM`**: Constant integer literal (`struct narithnum`).
  * **Unary Operators** (`struct narithunary`):
    * `A_PAREN` (parenthesized expression)
    * `A_UNARYMINUS`, `A_UNARYPLUS`, `A_NOT` (`!`), `A_BNOT` (`~`)
    * `A_PREDECR`, `A_PREINCR`, `A_POSTDECR`, `A_POSTINCR`
  * **Binary Operators** (`struct narithbinary`):
    * Logical: `A_OR` (`||`), `A_AND` (`&&`)
    * Bitwise: `A_BITOR` (`|`), `A_BITXOR` (`^`), `A_BITAND` (`&`)
    * Comparison: `A_EQ` (`==`), `A_NE` (`!=`), `A_LT` (`<`), `A_GT` (`>`), `A_GE` (`>=`), `A_LE` (`<=`)
    * Shift: `A_SHL` (`<<`), `A_SHR` (`>>`)
    * Arithmetic: `A_ADD` (`+`), `A_SUB` (`-`), `A_MUL` (`*`), `A_DIV` (`/`), `A_MOD` (`%`), `A_EXP` (`**`)
    * Assignment: `A_VASSIGN` (`=`), `A_VADD` (`+=`), `A_VSUB` (`-=`), `A_VMUL` (`*=`), `A_VDIV` (`/=`), `A_VMOD` (`%=`), `A_VSHL` (`<<=`), `A_VSHR` (`>>=`), `A_VBITAND` (`&=`), `A_VBITXOR` (`^=`), `A_VBITOR` (`|=`)
  
  ---
  
  ## 2. Common Node Prefix Layout
  
  Every node structure shares a mandatory prefix layout:
  
  ```c
  struct {
    enum kind id;       /* Node type identifier */
    unsigned bgnd : 1;  /* 1 bit flag: run in background (&) (or dummy : 1 in subnodes) */
    union node* next;   /* Pointer to the next node in the linked list */
  };
  ```
  
  Because `union node` overlays all struct types, any `union node* ptr` can safely access `ptr->id`, `ptr->bgnd`, and `ptr->next`.
  
  ---
  
  ## 3. Node Struct Definitions & Details
  
  ### Command Nodes
  
  #### `struct ncmd` (`N_SIMPLECMD`)
  Represents a simple command invocation.
  ```c
  struct ncmd {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned bgnd : 1;  /* Run in background (&) */
    union node* next;   /* Next command in chain */
    union node* rdir;   /* Redirections list (N_REDIR) */
    union node* vars;   /* Command-local variable assignments (N_ASSIGN) */
    union node* args;   /* Command arguments list (N_ARG) */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct npipe` (`N_PIPELINE`)
  Represents commands connected via pipes (`|`).
  ```c
  struct npipe {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    unsigned ncmd;      /* Number of commands in pipeline */
    union node* cmds;   /* Linked list of pipeline commands */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nnot` (`N_NOT`)
  Negates the exit status of a command pipeline (`! pipeline`).
  ```c
  struct nnot {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned dummy : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* pipeline;
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nandor` (`N_AND`, `N_OR`)
  Represents conditional logical execution (`&&` / `||`).
  ```c
  struct nandor {
    enum kind id;       /* N_AND or N_OR */
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* left;   /* Left operand command */
    union node* right;  /* Right operand command */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct ngrp` (`N_SUBSHELL`, `N_BRACEGROUP`)
  Grouping constructs `( list )` or `{ list; }`.
  ```c
  struct ngrp {
    enum kind id;       /* N_SUBSHELL or N_BRACEGROUP */
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* rdir;   /* Redirections applied to whole group */
    union node* cmds;   /* Body command list */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nfor` (`N_FOR`)
  Represents `for var in args; do cmds; done`.
  ```c
  struct nfor {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* rdir;   /* Redirections */
    union node* cmds;   /* Loop body */
    union node* args;   /* Argument list (N_ARG) */
    char* varn;         /* Loop variable name */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct ncase` & `struct ncasenode` (`N_CASE`, `N_CASENODE`)
  Case control statement and individual pattern clauses (`pattern) cmds ;;`).
  ```c
  struct ncase {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* rdir;   /* Redirections */
    union node* list;   /* Linked list of N_CASENODE clauses */
    union node* word;   /* Word evaluated for pattern match */
  };
  
  struct ncasenode {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned dummy : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* pats;   /* Pattern word list */
    union node* cmds;   /* Commands executed if matched */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nif` (`N_IF`)
  If-then-else construct.
  ```c
  struct nif {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* rdir;   /* Redirections */
    union node* cmd0;   /* On-true branch (then) */
    union node* cmd1;   /* On-false / elif branch (else) */
    union node* test;   /* Test condition command list */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nloop` (`N_WHILE`, `N_UNTIL`)
  Looping constructs.
  ```c
  struct nloop {
    enum kind id;       /* N_WHILE or N_UNTIL */
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* rdir;   /* Redirections */
    union node* cmds;   /* Loop body */
    union node* test;   /* Loop condition test */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nfunc` (`N_FUNCTION`)
  Function definition (`name() body`).
  ```c
  struct nfunc {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned dummy : 1;
    struct nfunc* next;
    char* name;         /* Function name */
    union node* body;   /* Function body AST */
    struct location loc;/* Source file position */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nlist` (`N_LIST`)
  Simple command list wrapper.
  ```c
  struct nlist {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned bgnd : 1;
    union node* next;
    union node* rdir;
    union node* cmds;
  };
  ```
  
  ---
  
  ### Word, Parameter & Redirection Nodes
  
  #### `struct narg` (`N_ARG`, `N_ASSIGN`)
  A shell word argument or variable assignment statement.
  ```c
  struct narg {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned flag;      /* Argument flags (e.g. ARG_QUOTED, ARG_ASSIGN) */
    union node* next;   /* Next argument in list */
    stralloc stra;      /* Pre-allocated string buffer if applicable */
    union node* list;   /* Linked list of word sub-segments (N_ARGSTR, N_ARGPARAM, etc.) */
  };
  ```
  
  #### `struct nredir` (`N_REDIR`)
  Redirection specification (`[fd]<op><target>`).
  ```c
  struct nredir {
    enum kind id;
    unsigned flag;      /* Redirection operator flag (from src/redir.h) */
    union node* next;
    union node* word;   /* File target, descriptor number, or delimiter word */
    union node* data;   /* Here-document content / expansion AST */
    int fdes;           /* File descriptor number (e.g. 0, 1, 2) */
    struct fd* fd;      /* Runtime FD state tracking pointer */
  };
  ```
  *Redirection Flags (`src/redir.h`)*:
  * `REDIR_OUTPUT` (`>`), `REDIR_CLOBBER` (`>|`), `REDIR_APPEND` (`>>`)
  * `REDIR_INPUT` (`<`), `REDIR_READWRITE` (`<>`)
  * `REDIR_HEREDOC` (`<<`), `REDIR_HEREDOC_TAB` (`<<-`)
  * `REDIR_DUPINPUT` (`<&`), `REDIR_DUPOUTPUT` (`>&`)
  
  #### Word Subnode Types (`list` children of `N_ARG`)
  
  * **`struct nargstr` (`N_ARGSTR`)**: Literal string or quoted segment.
    * Fields: `id`, `flag` (`ARG_QUOTED`, `ARG_SQ`, `ARG_DQ`, etc.), `next`, `stra` / `{char* str; size_t len;}`, `loc`.
  * **`struct nargparam` (`N_ARGPARAM`)**: Parameter expansion (`$VAR`, `${VAR: -default}`, `${#VAR}`, etc.).
    * Fields: `id`, `flag` (`PARAM_LENGTH`, `PARAM_DEFAULT`, `PARAM_ASSIGN`, etc.), `next`, `name`, `word`, `numb`, `loc`.
  * **`struct nargcmd` (`N_ARGCMD`)**: Command substitution `` `cmds` `` or `$(cmds)`.
    * Fields: `id`, `flag`, `next`, `list` (AST of commands to execute).
  * **`struct nargarith` (`N_ARGARITH`)**: Arithmetic substitution `$((expr))`.
    * Fields: `id`, `flag`, `next`, `tree` (Arithmetic AST expression tree).
  
  ---
  
  ### Arithmetic Subnode Types
  
  * **`struct narithnum` (`A_NUM`)**: Constant integer literal (`int64 num`, `unsigned base`).
  * **`struct narithunary`** (Unary/Parens): `id`, `dummy:1`, `next`, `union node* node`.
  * **`struct narithbinary`** (Binary/Assignment): `id`, `dummy:1`, `next`, `union node* left`, `union node* right`.
  
  ---
  
  ## 4. Node Memory Allocation & Dynamic Sizing
  
  * **Node Sizes Table**: `extern const int tree_nodesizes[]` (defined in `src/tree/tree_node.c`) specifies the exact memory size in bytes for every `enum kind`.
  * **Allocation**: `tree_newnode(enum kind nod)` allocates appropriate memory sized by `tree_nodesizes[nod]` and initializes `id`.
  
  ---
  
  ## 5. Tree Pointer Manipulation Macros
  
  `src/tree.h` provides key macros for manipulating singly-linked AST node lists using indirect pointers (`union node**`):
  
  | Macro | Description |
  | :--- | :--- |
  | `tree_init(node, nptr)` | Clears `node` to `NULL` and sets `nptr = &node`. |
  | `tree_link(node, nptr)` | Appends `node` at `*nptr` and updates `nptr = &(node)->next`. |
  | `tree_unshift(node, nptr)`| Prepends `node` to the front of `*nptr`. |
  | `tree_move(node, nptr)` | Moves `node` into `*nptr`, updates `nptr = &(node)->next`, and sets `node = NULL`. |
  | `tree_next(nptr)` | Obtains address of the `next` pointer of the node at `*nptr`. |
  | `tree_skip(nptr)` | Advances indirect pointer `nptr` to `&((*nptr)->next)`. |
